<!-- "Cosmic Luxury" palette, chosen by him on 09/12/2026. Replaced the Material 3 baseline
     dark theme from brief 241, whose #D0BCFF purple he rejected: "it looks too much like
     AI, too generic." And he was right: saturated magenta/purple on dark became the uniform
     of every AI product since 2024, and an app that sells itself as the one that does NOT
     make things up can't look like the ones that do.

     HIS RULE, and it's about PROPORTION, not inventory: cosmic_black + celestial_gold dominate
     50 to 60% of any screen. The secondary colors exist for what needs to pop, but they're a
     minority and derive from the same family (no Material traffic-light scheme, which is
     just as generic).

     PROVENANCE, line by line:
       cosmic_black #080A0F and celestial_gold #D4B16A came LITERALLY from the screenshot he sent
       (carousel "Color Palette #70 · Cosmic Luxury Edition", ui.ux.palette profile).
       Everything else is derived: cool neutrals in the dark, warm text in the gold family.

     CALCULATED CONTRASTS (WCAG), with the surface as background:
       text 15.34:1 · secondary_text 9.40:1 · primary 9.71:1 · warning 8.75:1
       · success 8.39:1 · error 5.09:1 · outline 3.33:1 (graphic AA; outline carries no text)
       text over high_container 11.89:1 · black over the gold 9.71:1 -->
